@description "Resilience: timeout and retry wrap the action; || guarantees a floor"

# :timeout and :retry are inheritable policy modifiers. They wrap the
# handler with a deadline and a bounded retry loop. || is a structural
# fallback: if everything on the left fails, the right branch runs.
#
# Three independent layers, each removable without touching the others.
# This is the production shape: fast-fail on transient upstream, always
# answer to the caller.

@assert: result == "recovered"

runtime.fail:timeout=100ms:retry=2 @{
  kind: "Timeout",
  message: "upstream slow",
}
|| const @{ value: "recovered" }
